AI Web Development Cohort 2: Full Curriculum
Vixora Academy · 12 weeks · Draft v1 for review
Course Overview
This course teaches students to build and launch real websites and web apps using modern web fundamentals together with AI coding tools. Students first learn HTML, CSS and JavaScript so they understand what they are building, then use vibe coding and AI assistants to build faster, add features, connect databases and AI, and deploy live projects. The course ends with a full capstone site or app and a freelancing-ready portfolio.
* Duration: 12 weeks
* Format: Online / Physical (hybrid)
* Level: Beginner (no prior coding required)
* Pricing: ₦30,000
* Certificate: Awarded on completion of the capstone project
Learning Outcomes
By the end of the course, students will be able to:
* Explain how websites and web apps work
* Build responsive pages with HTML, CSS and JavaScript
* Use AI coding tools to plan, build, debug and improve code, and check what the AI produces
* Build landing pages and multi-page sites quickly
* Build a simple React front end
* Store and retrieve data with a basic backend and database
* Add AI features to an app through an API
* Deploy a site with a domain and hosting
* Present their work and win freelance projects
Tools Used
VS Code, browser developer tools, Git and GitHub, AI coding assistants and vibe coding tools (such as Claude, ChatGPT, Cursor or similar), React, a hosted database service, and free deployment platforms. Specific tools may change, and free tiers are used wherever possible.
Course Structure
* Phase 1: Foundations (Weeks 1-3): how the web works, HTML, CSS
* Phase 2: Programming and AI Tools (Weeks 4-6): JavaScript, interactivity, vibe coding
* Phase 3: Building Real Projects (Weeks 7-10): landing pages, React, backend and databases, APIs and AI features
* Phase 4: Launch and Career (Weeks 11-12): deployment, capstone, portfolio, freelancing
Assessment (Proposed)
* Weekly build assignments
* Mid-course project: a responsive multi-section website
* Capstone project: a full website or web app, deployed live
* Certificate issued on completing all weekly deliverables and the capstone
Week 1: How the Web Works and Tools Setup
Objectives
* Understand how websites reach a browser
* Set up a professional coding workspace
Topics
* Browsers, servers, domains and hosting, in plain language
* Front end versus back end
* Setting up VS Code and useful extensions
* Browser developer tools
* Git and GitHub basics: repositories, commits and pushing code
Hands-on
* Set up the workspace and publish a first page to GitHub
Deliverable: GitHub account with a first repository
Week 2: HTML and Structuring Pages
Objectives
* Build the structure of a web page
* Write clean, accessible HTML
Topics
* HTML document structure and common tags
* Headings, text, lists, links and images
* Forms and inputs
* Semantic HTML and accessibility basics
* Planning a page before coding
Hands-on
* Build a personal profile page and a simple business page with a contact form
Deliverable: two HTML pages in GitHub
Week 3: CSS and Styling
Objectives
* Style pages so they look professional
* Build layouts that work on every screen size
Topics
* CSS selectors, colors, fonts and spacing (the box model)
* Flexbox and Grid
* Responsive design and media queries
* Basic design principles: hierarchy, contrast and consistency
* Typography and image handling
Hands-on
* Style the Week 2 pages into a responsive, polished site
Deliverable: responsive styled website
Week 4: JavaScript Basics
Objectives
* Understand core programming ideas
* Write basic JavaScript
Topics
* Variables, data types and operators
* Conditionals and loops
* Functions
* Arrays and objects
* Reading and fixing errors in the console
Hands-on
* Write small programs: a tip calculator and a quiz
Deliverable: JavaScript practice exercises
Week 5: JavaScript for Interactivity
Objectives
* Make pages respond to users
* Work with the page through the DOM
Topics
* The DOM: selecting and changing elements
* Events: clicks, input and form submission
* Form validation
* Fetching data from an API
* Saving small amounts of data in the browser
Hands-on
* Build a to-do app and a weather or quote app that loads live data
Deliverable: two interactive mini apps
Week 6: Vibe Coding and AI Coding Tools
Objectives
* Build with AI as a coding partner
* Stay in control of the code
Topics
* What vibe coding is, and where it works well and where it fails
* Writing clear build prompts: goal, features, style and constraints
* Breaking a project into steps for the AI
* Reading, testing and debugging AI-generated code
* Refactoring and asking AI to explain code
* Security and safety basics: never share secret keys, and review what you deploy
Hands-on
* Build a small app by prompting, then review and fix the code yourself
Deliverable: AI-built app with a prompt log and review notes
Week 7: Building Landing Pages with AI
Objectives
* Build high-quality landing pages fast
* Write page content that converts
Topics
* Landing page structure: hero, benefits, proof, offer and call to action
* Using AI to draft copy, layouts and code
* Images, icons and fonts
* Contact forms and lead capture
* Basic search visibility (SEO) and page speed
Hands-on
* Build a complete landing page for a real or sample business
Deliverable: landing page project (also the mid-course project)
Week 8: Frontend Frameworks: Introduction to React
Objectives
* Understand why frameworks exist
* Build a small React app
Topics
* Components, props and state
* JSX and rendering lists
* Handling events and forms
* Project structure and running a React project
* Using AI to help generate and explain React code
Hands-on
* Rebuild an earlier mini app in React
Deliverable: working React app
Week 9: Backend and Database Basics
Objectives
* Understand how apps store and serve data
* Connect a front end to a database
Topics
* What a backend is and how front end and back end talk
* Databases: tables, records and simple queries
* Using a hosted database service
* Basic user accounts and authentication, at an introductory level
* Keeping data and keys safe
Hands-on
* Add saving and loading of data to an app
Deliverable: app that stores and retrieves data
Week 10: APIs and AI Integration
Objectives
* Use APIs to add features to an app
* Add an AI feature safely
Topics
* What APIs are, and reading API documentation
* Making API requests and handling responses
* Adding an AI feature (such as a chatbot or text generator) through an API
* Protecting API keys with environment variables
* Costs and limits
Hands-on
* Add an AI-powered feature to an existing app
Deliverable: app with a working AI feature
Week 11: Deployment, Domains and Hosting, with Capstone Build
Objectives
* Put a project live on the internet
* Make solid progress on the capstone
Topics
* Deploying with free hosting platforms
* Connecting a custom domain
* Environment variables and configuration in production
* Testing and fixing bugs before launch
* Capstone planning and build sessions with instructor check-ins
Hands-on
* Deploy a project live
* Build the capstone
Deliverable: deployed project and capstone in progress
Week 12: Capstone Presentation, Portfolio and Freelancing
Objectives
* Present the capstone with confidence
* Leave ready to take on clients
Topics
* Final capstone presentations and feedback
* Building a portfolio site and GitHub profile
* Finding clients: freelance platforms, LinkedIn and local businesses
* Writing proposals and pricing web projects
* Contracts, deadlines and client communication basics
Hands-on
* Present the capstone live
* Publish the portfolio site
Deliverable: final capstone and live portfolio
Capstone Project Requirements (Proposed)
* A real or realistic problem and a short project brief
* A responsive, deployed website or web app
* At least one dynamic feature (data storage or an AI feature)
* Code on GitHub with a clear README
* A prompt log or short note on how AI was used and checked
* A 10-minute live demo and presentation